                   [--worker-index WORKER_INDEX]\n                        [--gate-trigger GATE_TRIGGER]\n                        [--gate-reason GATE_REASON]\n\nAppend one memory event, or atomically rewrite conclusions.md.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --write-conclusions   Switch into conclusions-write mode (validates and\n                        replaces conclusions.md).\n  --event-json EVENT_JSON\n                        Event payload as JSON object string\n  --event-file EVENT_FILE\n                        Path to event JSON file\n  --local-memory-md LOCAL_MEMORY_MD\n                        Local workspace memory markdown path\n  --global-memory-md GLOBAL_MEMORY_MD\n                        Global markdown memory path (event mode)\n  --global-memory-jsonl GLOBAL_MEMORY_JSONL\n                        Global JSONL memory path (event mode)\n  --conclusions-md CONCLUSIONS_MD\n                        Path of conclusions.md to overwrite (--write-\n                        conclusions mode)\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_JSONL\n                        Path of conclusions_history.jsonl to append a record\n                        to\n  --conclusions-text CONCLUSIONS_TEXT\n                        Conclusion paragraph (omit to read from stdin)\n  --cycle-index CYCLE_INDEX\n                        Current cycle index for the history record\n  --worker-index WORKER_INDEX\n                        Current worker index for the history record\n  --gate-trigger GATE_TRIGGER\n                        Gate trigger letter (a|b|c|d) recorded in history\n  --gate-reason GATE_REASON\n                        One-sentence reason for the update; for trigger d name\n                        the dimension\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'Linear|AdamW|one_hot|manual_seed|num_threads|betas|def train|def neural' task/evaluate.py; ls task/resources; ls ../investigation; ls ../final_evaluation/results; cat task/program_0/program_spec.toml; cat task/requirements.txt; sed -n '1,115p' task/program_0/src/program.py; cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json')); d=s['\"'$defs'\"']['LegacyFigureManifestFigure'];print('LEGACY',list(d['properties']));print('req',d['required'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'Linear|AdamW|one_hot|manual_seed|num_threads|betas|def train|def neural' task/evaluate.py; ls task/resources; ls ../investigation; ls ../final_evaluation/results; cat task/program_0/program_spec.toml; cat task/requirements.txt; sed -n '1,115p' task/program_0/src/program.py; cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json')); d=s['\"'$defs'\"']['LegacyFigureManifestFigure'];print('LEGACY',list(d['properties']));print('req',d['required'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"789:def training_worker(repair):\n796:    torch.set_num_threads(1)\n803:        return functional.one_hot(pairs, 97).reshape(-1, 194).float()\n826:            torch.manual_seed(request[\"seed\"])\n828:            model = torch.nn.Sequential(torch.nn.Linear(194, width), torch.nn.ReLU(), torch.nn.Linear(width, 97))\n846:                     \"optimizer\": torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=.001, weight_decay=request[\"decay\"],\n847:                                                    betas=(.9, .999), eps=1e-8, foreach=False, fused=False)}\n954:            def train_call(request):\nfinal\nsearch\n_idea_generation\nattempts_history.jsonl\nbest_program_manifest.json\nconclusions.md\nconclusions_history.jsonl\nconclusions_other_workers.md\nevents.jsonl\nidea_generation_failures.jsonl\nideas\nideas_history.jsonl\nlatest_run_manifest.json\nmemory.jsonl\nmemory.md\nouter_state.json\ntask\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nmetrics.json\nschema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".venv/**\",\n  \"node_modules/**\",\n  \".git/**\",\n  \".mypy_cache/**\",\n  \".pytest_cache/**\",\n  \".ruff_cache/**\",\n  \".tox/**\",\n  \".nox/**\",\n  \"dist/**\",\n  \"build/**\",\n]\ninclude = [\n]\n\n[integration]\nkind = \"generic\"\nnotes = \"\"\nnumpy==2.1.3\ntorch==2.5.1+cpu\n\"\"\"Deterministic shared learning-rate controller for evaluator-owned neural training.\n\nEntrypoint: handle(request) -> response, finite JSON objects only. Exactly the\ndocumented keys are accepted and returned; additional response keys are forbidden.\nThere are no tensors, paths, state transfers, binary data, or implicit RPC calls.\nState is reset for every episode and remains in candidate-owned memory only.\n\nreset: {\"op\":\"reset\",\"seed\":integer >=0} -> {\"ok\":true}. Seeds initialize\nrandomness only, never workload or plane identity. Accept arbitrary valid seeds.\nClears all state. This is always the first request of an episode.\n\nrecipe: {\"op\":\"recipe\",\"steps\":positive integer,\"block_steps\":positive\ninteger dividing steps,\"min_lr\":0.0001,\"max_lr\":0.01} ->\n{\"initial_lr\":number in [0.0001,0.01],\"decay_rate\":number in [0.01,1]}.\nCalled once after reset. The SAME numeric recipe must apply across every seed,\nwidth, operation and decay arm; reset seeds must not select recipes. Public\nworkload fields have identical meanings in all planes and smoke. The evaluator\nowns a 194-input, width-[16,64,256] ReLU MLP with 97 logits, AdamW, CE, full-batch\ntraining and all data. Candidate controls only this bounded learning-rate family.\n\nschedule: {\"op\":\"schedule\",\"step\":integer in [0,steps),\"steps\":positive\ninteger,\"block_steps\":positive integer} -> {\"lr\":finite number}. After recipe,\ncalled in increasing steps 0,block_steps,...,steps-block_steps. Return exactly\nmax(0.0001,min(0.01,initial_lr*decay_rate**(step/steps))) within absolute 1e-12.\nEach rate governs one evaluator-owned block of optimizer updates. Workload must\nmatch recipe; no observations, scores, targets, outcomes or feedback enter RPC.\nAt production workload steps=20000,block_steps=500, 42 calls per episode: reset,\nrecipe,40 schedule. Smoke reduces steps and block_steps only. No replay. Search\neligibility tests complete, genuine training and controls, NOT a favorable size\ntrend or a performance margin. Null and negative scientific results are valid.\n\nSearch ranks the mean accuracy of the last five heldout checkpoints, averaged\nequally across seeds, widths, decays and operations. An episode failure scores 0\nin the original denominator. Evaluation never trusts candidate internal flags.\nAll messages including JSON framing must be below 16 KiB here (and 64 MiB wire).\nImplementations cannot supply code, weights, labels or artifact paths to training.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\n_state = None\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    global _state\n    if type(request) is not dict:\n        raise ValueError(\"request must be an object\")\n    operation = request.get(\"op\")\n    if operation == \"reset\":\n        if set(request) != {\"op\", \"seed\"} or type(request[\"seed\"]) is not int or request[\"seed\"] < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid reset\")\n        _state = {}\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if _state is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"reset required\")\n    if operation == \"recipe\":\n        if set(request) != {\"op\", \"steps\", \"block_steps\", \"min_lr\", \"max_lr\"}:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid recipe fields\")\n        steps, block_steps = request[\"steps\"], request[\"block_steps\"]\n        if type(steps) is not int or type(block_steps) is not int or block_steps <= 0 or steps <= 0 or steps % block_steps:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid workload\")\n        if request[\"min_lr\"] != .0001 or request[\"max_lr\"] != .01 or _state:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid recipe state\")\n        _state = {\"steps\": steps, \"block_steps\": block_steps, \"next_step\": 0,\n                  \"initial_lr\": .001, \"decay_rate\": 1.0}\n        return {\"initial_lr\": _state[\"initial_lr\"], \"decay_rate\": _state[\"decay_rate\"]}\n    if operation == \"schedule\":\n        if set(request) != {\"op\", \"step\", \"steps\", \"block_steps\"} or not _state:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid schedule fields\")\n        if any(type(request[key]) is not int or request[key] != _state[key if key != \"step\" else \"next_step\"]\n               for key in (\"step\", \"steps\", \"block_steps\")) or request[\"step\"] >= _state[\"steps\"]:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid schedule state\")\n        rate = max(.0001, min(.01, _state[\"initial_lr\"] * _state[\"decay_rate\"] ** (request[\"step\"] / request[\"steps\"])))\n        if not math.isfinite(rate):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid rate\")\n        _state[\"next_step\"] += _state[\"block_steps\"]\n        return {\"lr\": rate}\n    raise ValueError(\"unknown operation\")\n{\n  \"$id\": \"https://schemas.agentic-scientist.local/scientific-evidence/artifact-manifest.schema.json\",\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"artifact\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"source\",\n            \"derived\",\n            \"manuscript\",\n            \"figure\",\n            \"table\",\n            \"script\",\n            \"log\",\n            \"other\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"media_type\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"description\": \"Path to the artifact relative to the scientific-evidence root when possible.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"sha256\": {\n          \"description\": \"Optional hash recorded when the producing workflow computes one.\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\"