{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_strategy.json'))\nfor x in p['figure_specs']:print(x['figure_id'],x['layout_rationale'])\nPY\ncat literature/2210.01117.txt; sed -n '70,105p' iclr2026_conference.sty; rg -n 'json_pointer|locator|stable|id:' .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py | tail -40; sed -n '1,65p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh; head -45 .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_strategy.json'))\nfor x in p['figure_specs']:print(x['figure_id'],x['layout_rationale'])\nPY\ncat literature/2210.01117.txt; sed -n '70,105p' iclr2026_conference.sty; rg -n 'json_pointer|locator|stable|id:' .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py | tail -40; sed -n '1,65p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh; head -45 .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"study_overview The inspected ICLR style has one 5.5-inch text column, not a two-column layout. Two adjacent schematic compartments need the entire 5.5-inch width; a nominal half-width rendering would be only 2.75 inches and force tiny labels. Target 1.7-2.0 inches of graphic height plus caption, about 0.3 body page, on page 1 or 2.\nwidth_decay_outcomes Four panels in two rows and two columns fit the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width at approximately 2.5 inches per panel after gutters. Target 3.1-3.5 inches graphic height plus caption, about 0.45 body page. Separate row scales prevent near-zero held-out values from disappearing under the training-accuracy range; scales match across operations within each row. Do not shrink a four-panel figure to half text width.\ncensoring_audit Two side-by-side panels need the full 5.5-inch text width so capped observations, a shared legend, and the non-attainment annotation remain legible at 9-point text. Target 2.0-2.3 inches graphic height plus caption, about 0.3 body page. Use a visibly labeled focused vertical range covering the observed capped values; never imply a zero origin or an observed event at the cap.\nTitle: Omnigrok: Grokking Beyond Algorithmic Data\nAuthors: Liu, Ziming; Michaud, Eric J.; Tegmark, Max\nSource: https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.01117\n\nAbstract consulted:\nGrokking, the unusual phenomenon for algorithmic datasets where generalization happens long after overfitting the training data, has remained elusive. We aim to understand grokking by analyzing the loss landscapes of neural networks, identifying the mismatch between training and test losses as the cause for grokking. We refer to this as the \"LU mechanism\" because training and test losses (against model weight norm) typically resemble \"L\" and \"U\", respectively. This simple mechanism can nicely explain many aspects of grokking: data size dependence, weight decay dependence, the emergence of representations, etc. Guided by the intuitive picture, we are able to induce grokking on tasks involving images, language and molecules. In the reverse direction, we are able to eliminate grokking for algorithmic datasets. We attribute the dramatic nature of grokking for algorithmic datasets to representation learning.\n   \\@maketitle \\@thanks\n\\endgroup\n\\setcounter{footnote}{0}\n\\let\\maketitle\\relax \\let\\@maketitle\\relax\n\\gdef\\@thanks{}\\gdef\\@author{}\\gdef\\@title{}\\let\\thanks\\relax}\n\n% The toptitlebar has been raised to top-justify the first page\n\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhead{}\n\n% Title (includes both anonimized and non-anonimized versions)\n\\def\\@maketitle{\\vbox{\\hsize\\textwidth\n%\\linewidth\\hsize \\vskip 0.1in \\toptitlebar \\centering\n{\\LARGE\\sc \\@title\\par}\n%\\bottomtitlebar % \\vskip 0.1in %  minus\n\\ificlrfinal\n    \\lhead{Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2026}\n    \\def\\And{\\end{tabular}\\hfil\\linebreak[0]\\hfil\n            \\begin{tabular}[t]{l}\\bf\\rule{\\z@}{24pt}\\ignorespaces}%\n  \\def\\AND{\\end{tabular}\\hfil\\linebreak[4]\\hfil\n            \\begin{tabular}[t]{l}\\bf\\rule{\\z@}{24pt}\\ignorespaces}%\n    \\begin{tabular}[t]{l}\\bf\\rule{\\z@}{24pt}\\@author\\end{tabular}%\n\\else\n       \\lhead{Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2026}\n   \\def\\And{\\end{tabular}\\hfil\\linebreak[0]\\hfil\n            \\begin{tabular}[t]{l}\\bf\\rule{\\z@}{24pt}\\ignorespaces}%\n  \\def\\AND{\\end{tabular}\\hfil\\linebreak[4]\\hfil\n            \\begin{tabular}[t]{l}\\bf\\rule{\\z@}{24pt}\\ignorespaces}%\n    \\begin{tabular}[t]{l}\\bf\\rule{\\z@}{24pt}Anonymous authors\\\\Paper under double-blind review\\end{tabular}%\n\\fi\n\\vskip 0.3in minus 0.1in}}\n\n\\renewenvironment{abstract}{\\vskip.075in\\centerline{\\large\\sc\nAbstract}\\vspace{0.5ex}\\begin{quote}}{\\par\\end{quote}\\vskip 1ex}\n111:    locator: str | None\n184:            \"description\": \"Target path, URI, or stable identifier before the optional #locator.\",\n190:        \"locator\": {\n193:            \"description\": \"Opaque locator fragment after #. The base verifier does not need universal parsing.\",\n266:            \"description\": \"Inline @evidence refs or stable ids describing the artifact inputs.\",\n292:            \"locator\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n344:            \"locator\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n438:            \"Target        := non-empty path | absolute path | URI | stable identifier\",\n461:            \"- `resolved`: the target exists and the verifier can validate the locator semantics it understands.\",\n462:            \"- `anchored`: the target exists, but only path/hash checks were possible or the locator remained opaque.\",\n471:            \"5. Do not pretend to interpret unknown locator grammars. Keep them `anchored` unless an adapter proves more.\",\n479:            \"- resolve refs against real files or stable ids\",\n628:    target, locator = inner.split(\"#\", 1) if \"#\" in inner else (inner, None)\n630:    compact_locator = locator.strip() if locator is not None else None\n636:        locator=compact_locator or None,\n727:    if parsed.locator is not None:\n728:        payload[\"locator\"] = parsed.locator\n757:        status = \"resolved\" if parsed.locator is None else \"anchored\"\n759:        if parsed.locator is not None:\n760:            message = \"Ledger id exists, but locator semantics were not interpreted by the base verifier.\"\n794:        if parsed.locator is None:\n803:            messages=(\"Target path exists, but locator semantics were not interpreted by the base verifier.\",),\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" bibtex \\\n  --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --aux \"$AUX_FILE\"\nrun_sanitized bibtex \"$BASE\"\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated claim-grounding artifacts before paper finalization.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nKEY_RE = re.compile(r\"@\\w+\\{([^,]+),\")\nEVIDENCE_REF_RE = re.compile(r\"@evidence\\[\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\]\")\nTEX_INPUT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\\s*\"\n    r\"(?:\\{(?P<braced>[^{}]+)\\}|(?P<unbraced>[^\\s%{}]+))\"\n)\nTEX_IMPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?P<command>usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)\"\n    r\"(?![A-Za-z@])(?:\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\s*\\{(?P<targets>[^{}]+)\\}\"\n)\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)(?![A-Za-z@])\"\n)\nDYNAMIC_TEX_IMPORT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\csname\\s*(?:input|include)\\s*\\\\endcsname\")\nCONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\if[a-zA-Z@]+\\b|\\\\else\\b|\\\\fi\\b\")\nVERBATIM_ENV_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?P<env>verbatim\\*?|lstlisting|minted)\\}.*?\"\n    r\"\\\\end\\s*\\{(?P=env)\\}\",\n    re.DOTALL,\n)\nPROMPT_ARTIFACT_RE = re.compile(r\".+_prompt(?:_round_\\d+(?:_contract_retry_\\d+)?)?\\.md$\")\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\n    \"validation_feedback.json\",\n    \"validation_feedback.md\",\n    \"verification-report.json\",\n}\nROOT_GENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\"validation_report.json\"}\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_PREFIXES = (\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
