4.30265273/sqrt(3), clipped to [-H,H]; its degeneracy follows from zero contrast variation.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.width_lag_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"source_files\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:762\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The supplementary table preserves all 36 records' event times, capped lags, and final-five-checkpoint accuracies; the diagnostic table averages final-checkpoint training CE, held-out CE, and parameter norm over the three seeds for each condition.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"derived_artifacts\\\": [\\\"tables/full_observations.tex\\\", \\\"tables/diagnostics.tex\\\"],\n+      \\\"source_files\\\": [\\\"build_artifacts.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:805\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The three stored seed-evaluation durations, each covering its condition grid, are 786.393,777.546,786.875 seconds; they are observations, not portable runtime guarantees.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"evidence_locator\\\": \\\"/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/*/duration_seconds\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The independent final qualification sources report completed, qualified, and true; this acceptance does not establish generalization or a neural mechanism. The retained diagnostics-trust designation is unverified.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"evidence_locator\\\": \\\"/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/candidate_diagnostics_trust\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No matched final-plane comparison to the original lower-rate recipe is retained; development scores are not used as final results, and no cross-task transfer, random-label training, initial-logit calibration, circuit measurement, or generalization-time equivalence is claimed.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"source_files\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/controller/src/EXPERIMENT_SCOPE.md\\\", \\\"source_evidence/controller/src/program.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The final evaluator and observation-file hashes match their final metadata; hashes identify supplied artifacts rather than prove implementation substance.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"source_files\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluation_evidence.json\\\", \\\"source_evidence/final_manifest.json\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Grokking can produce held-out improvement long after training-set fitting on small algorithmic datasets, with dataset size affecting optimization requirements.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.arxiv.2201.02177\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Power2022GrokkingGB\\\"],\n+      \\\"source_files\\\": [\\\"literature/2201.02177.txt\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"AdamW decouples weight decay from the loss-gradient update; the fixed-rate shrinkage contribution (1-eta*lambda)\"'^t is not the full trained parameter trajectory.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.1711.05101\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/1711.05101.txt\", \"source_evidence/controller/src/EXPERIMENT_SCOPE.md\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"Omnigrok discusses weight-norm loss landscapes and grokking beyond algorithmic data; those mechanisms are comparator context, not measured conclusions of this study.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2210.01117\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Liu2023Omnigrok\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/2210.01117.txt\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"Circuit efficiency proposes competition between memorizing and generalizing solutions with different learning speeds and norm efficiency; the present experiment does not measure that mechanism.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2309.02390\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Varma2023ExplainingGT\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/2309.02390.txt\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"Lazy-to-rich dynamics is an analyzed grokking account including a two-layer polynomial-regression setting; no kernel or feature-learning diagnostic is measured here.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2310.06110\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Kumar2024LazyRich\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/2310.06110.txt\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"Unifying Grokking and Double Descent proposes a pattern-learning-speed account including variation in model capacity; this work does not establish double descent.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.2303.06173\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Davies2023Unifying\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/2303.06173.txt\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"Deep Double Descent reports nonmonotone performance with model size and training duration in other settings; the present sparse grid does not infer a general width law.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.1912.02292\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Nakkiran2020DoubleDescent\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/1912.02292.txt\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"Fitting labels and explaining generalization are distinct problems, as illustrated by random-label fitting results in the cited literature, not independently executed in this study.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"ref.arxiv.1611.03530\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [\"Zhang2017Rethinking\"],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"literature/1611.03530.txt\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"claim\": \"LLMs contributed to proposals, bounded controller implementation, query planning, framing, analysis code, writing and grounding; the training computation owns the retained numerical observations.\",\n+      \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"],\n+      \"citation_keys\": [],\n+      \"source_files\": [\"source_evidence/controller/src/EXPERIMENT_SCOPE.md\", \"reference_query_plan.json\", \"paper_strategy.json\", \"build_artifacts.py\", \"memory.md\"]\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n+# Reproduction and evidence boundaries\n+\n+## Scope\n+\n+This bundle analyzes the retained final evaluation. It does not rerun training or\n+evaluate a new controller. The central result is finite-horizon memorization\n+without observed sustained generalization, not a generalization-time or mechanism\n+claim. `paper_data.json` is the unchanged host evidence registry.\n+\n+The final qualification sources independently report completed/qualified/true.\n+Acceptance does not imply generalization, superiority, or comprehensive validity\n+certification. The diagnostics trust flag remains unverified. The original\n+lower-rate configuration has no matched final evaluation here.\n+\n+## Neural training\n+\n+- Dependencies: `source_evidence/requirements.txt` pins NumPy and CPU PyTorch.\n+- Training implementation: `source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:789` owns feature\n+  construction, initialization, AdamW, full-batch cross-entropy, and checkpoints.\n+- Controller: `source_evidence/controller/program_spec.toml` points to\n+  `source_evidence/controller/src/program.py`. It returns a shared constant rate.\n+- Seeds: read the three seed entries in\n+  `paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes`.\n+- Data: `source_evidence/resources/final/benchmark.json` is retained. The exact\n+  generation and partition code is at `source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:588`.\n+  Data are synthetic and require no downloads, accounts, or third-party licenses.\n+- Measurements: `source_evidence/evaluation_evidence.json` and the corresponding\n+  embedded final records in `paper_data.json` are the retained observations.\n+\n+The original evaluator accepts `--program_path` and `--results_dir`, but depends\n+on an external RPC broker. A complete standalone broker launcher is not supplied.\n+These flags alone are not a working independent training reproduction command.\n+The source snapshots make the neural computation inspectable; replaying the full\n+execution context requires the original orchestration infrastructure. No new\n+training command or unmeasured runtime is invented to conceal this limitation.\n+\n+The recorded seed-evaluation durations are available in `analysis/derived_results.json`.\n+They are actual durations, not portable hardware/runtime estimates.\n+\n+## Recompute tables and quantitative figures\n+\n+Create analysis dependencies outside the manuscript tree:\n+\n+```sh\n+python -m venv /tmp/paper-analysis\n+/tmp/paper-analysis/bin/pip install -r analysis/plotting_requirements.txt\n+/tmp/paper-analysis/bin/python build_artifacts.py\n+```\n+\n+This reads final records, checks the event and lag computations against stored\n+values, and writes the following artifacts without training:\n+\n+| Paper artifact | Output | Source |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| Main event table | `tables/events.tex` | final observations, memorization/generalization fields |\n+| Complete seed table | `tables/full_observations.tex` | final traces and event fields |\n+| Endpoint diagnostics table | `tables/diagnostics.tex` | final checkpoint losses and parameter norms |\n+| Width/decay outcome figure | `figures/width_decay_outcomes.pdf`, `.png` | final five trace checkpoints |\n+| Censoring audit figure | `figures/censoring_audit.pdf`, `.png` | observed events and capped lags |\n+| Machine-readable derived results | `analysis/derived_results.json` | same final observations |\n+\n+All are produced by `build_artifacts.py`. Quantitative PDF exports are vector\n+graphics; PNGs are generated directly at 300 DPI on an 8.25-inch-wide canvas.\n+The concept overview is orchestrator-owned and initially contains a deliberately\n+labeled placeholder. The build script never overwrites a completed concept\n+figure or a figure with a nonempty rendering log. No artificial trajectories\n+or synthetic measurements are used.\n+\n+## Compile and check\n+\n+```sh\n+python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\n+python .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py '\"\\\\\n+  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\\\n+  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n+\"'```\n+\n+Compilation requires LaTeX, BibTeX and Poppler `pdftotext`. The official ICLR 2026\n+style and bibliography style were retrieved from the exact official template\n+directory; URLs and file hashes are retained in\n+`source_evidence/template_provenance.json`. Review mode remains anonymous.\n+\n+The bundled figure validator imports parent-only orchestration code. Where that\n+module is unavailable locally, schema/density checks are recorded separately and\n+the parent must run its authoritative figure and page-occupancy validator.\n+\n+## Literature safety and unmet reference quota\n+\n+Only the eight exact source identities approved by the strategy were retrieved\n+and consulted, at title/author/abstract scope. `literature/retrieve_approved.py`\n+contains that allowlist; `references_provenance.json` identifies the consulted\n+files and their provenance. No citation graphs, recommendations, or broad\n+width/grokking searches were consulted. Off-target metadata in the initial\n+retrieval was not used as substantive evidence. No prohibited identity was\n+inferred or intentionally accessed.\n+\n+The requested minimum of 25 references cannot be met under the strategy'\"'s\n+eight-identity safety boundary. The manuscript cites eight real consulted\n+sources rather than padding the bibliography with unrelated or unconsulted\n+entries. This is an explicit unresolved submission requirement, not a successful\n+reference-count validation. See \"'`submission_readiness.json` for final status.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_artifacts.py\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
