{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '60,102p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py; ls -ld /usr/share/texmf /usr/share/texmf/web2c /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf; readlink -f /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf; sed -n '1,35p' paper.fls; tail -15 /tmp/paper-apt.log; /tmp/paper-tools/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport fitz\np=fitz.open('paper.pdf');page=p[7]; print(page.get_text()[-2200:]);print('8th page rect',page.rect)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/tmp/paper-tools/lib/python3.12/site-packages/fitz/__init__.py:17: FutureWarning: The `fitz` API is deprecated and will be removed in future. Use `import pymupdf` instead.\n  warnings.warn(\n387\n388\n389\n390\n391\n392\n393\n394\n395\n396\n397\n398\n399\n400\n401\n402\n403\n404\n405\n406\n407\n408\n409\n410\n411\n412\n413\n414\n415\n416\n417\n418\n419\n420\n421\n422\n423\n424\n425\n426\n427\n428\n429\n430\n431\nSelection and evidence boundaries.\nThe fixed learning-rate recipe was selected using develop-\nment evidence. Only its final factorial is analyzed here; the absence of a matched final result for the\noriginal recipe precludes a final-baseline improvement claim. The recorded final evaluation com-\npleted and was accepted under its specified criteria. That acceptance certifies neither generalization\nnor a neural mechanism, and the retained metadata does not provide a comprehensive integrity or\nadaptivity audit. Claims are therefore tied to inspectable evaluator observations and readable imple-\nmentation snapshots rather than to acceptance labels or hashes alone.\n6\nCONCLUSION\nModel size can change the onset and attainability of training-set fitting without producing an ob-\nserved generalization transition.\nIn the evaluated modular addition and subtraction grid, wider\nfixed-rate ReLU networks memorize earlier without decay and overcome the narrowest models’\nfitting deficit with positive decay. Nevertheless, none of the 36 complete records reaches sustained\ngeneralization by 20,000 updates. The supported conclusion is a finite-horizon separation between\nfitting and held-out learning, not a claim that scale accelerates, prevents, or leaves unchanged even-\ntual grokking.\nThe distinction is consequential for measurement. An endpoint-substituted lag can display a nonzero\nwidth contrast with no seed variation even when its generalization event is never observed. Report-\ning event attainment, fitting times, and the observation boundary alongside that statistic is essential\nto its interpretation. A stronger account of width-dependent delayed generalization would need\nobserved transitions, more initialization and split replication, and controls separating width, initial-\nization scale, and regularization. Those measurements are not supplied here. The present evidence\ninstead establishes which part of the scale question can be answered within the measured budget,\nand which part remains unidentified.\n8\n\n8th page rect Rect(0.0, 0.0, 612.0, 792.0)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
