ly to the implemented capped summary and does not incorporate split variation or hyperparameter selection. We do not pool checkpoint measurements into extra replications, infer confidence from overlapping seed markers, or interpret a zero-width interval as robustness across unseen settings. Reusing a seed aligns the random-number initialization procedure, but differently shaped networks do not have identical initial functions. Likewise, the two operations share an algebraic family while having different fixed input partitions. Pairing improves the definition of a conditional comparison; it does not turn those observations into independent draws from a broad population of models or tasks.\n*** Update File: claims_grounding.json\n@@\n-  \\\"claims\\\": [\n+  \\\"claims\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"On addition, mean final held-out CE is 339.459 without decay versus 8.390 with decay at width 16, and 89.877 versus 8.627 at width 256. Loss differences do not establish generalization events or a mechanism.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"derived_artifact\\\": \\\"analysis/derived_results.json#/records\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The three-seed mean initial parameter norms are 6.288, 7.383, and 10.904 at widths 16, 64, and 256. Initial norms coincide across operation/decay arms at fixed width and seed, but widths are not norm-matched.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"source_files\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:825\\\"],\n+      \\\"derived_artifact\\\": \\\"analysis/derived_results.json#/records\\\"\n+    },\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py run -- pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex > analysis/latex_pass4.log 2>&1 && python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scrip